   "body": "**Adversarial review round 2 (Opus 5.5) — APPROVE** — head a5e3a849 (round 1: REQUEST CHANGES at 03c00c34)\n\n1. **low (optional)** — `ReaderInsetsWebTests.swift:184`: the reference `(contentOffset.y + inset)/zoomScale` is the same formula as `readingTop` + `layoutY`, so the test proves the zoom division is applied (the old one-liner fails it) and that `window.scrollTo` restores CSS px, not independently that this is the content under the bar. A JS position cannot serve (the page's `visualViewport` does not follow a native `setZoomScale`). Better reference: `scrollView.convert(CGPoint(x: 0, y: contentOffset.y + inset.top), to: viewForZooming)` (WKContentView, CSS px at scale 1). Not blocking.\n2. Round-1 findings: 1 resolved (the web test fails for the right reason: the old code saved 2300 scroll-view points, the reference is 1150); 2 resolved (the comment gives CSS px as the reason; the body's wording is correct); 3 unchanged, acceptable.\n3. Robustness: ±1 CSS px; `before` and `readingTop` read in the same main-actor turn; reachable offsets on a ~4500 px page; points only; the waits cover a late layout reset (#642).\n4. Rest of the diff: `readingTop` has one caller (`ReaderWebController.swift:133`); the restore path is unchanged; the pure tests and doc comments are correct.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
